<article class="env-lemma" id="05TR">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05TR">Lemma <span data-tag="05TR">13.26.4</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category. Let $u : A \to B$ be a strict monomorphism of $\text{Fil}^ f(\mathcal{A})$ and $f : A \to I$ a morphism from $A$ into a filtered injective object in $\text{Fil}^ f(\mathcal{A})$. Then there exists a morphism $g : B \to I$ such that $f = g \circ u$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The pushout $f' : I \to I \amalg _ A B$ of $f$ by $u$ is a strict monomorphism, see Homology, Lemma <a href="/tag/05SM" data-tag="05SM">12.19.10</a>. Hence the result follows formally from Lemma <a href="/tag/05TQ" data-tag="05TQ">13.26.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>